# The companion to 295: what the operand scope did NOT widen. Three
# restatements, each refused, each for the reason the scope rule gives.
#   line 15  LINEAR — two occurrences on the open lifeline with nothing but a
#            message between them. Unchanged since the rule was written.
#   line 20  SAME OPERAND — two occurrences inside one branch are consecutive
#            on that branch; exclusivity is between SIBLING operands, not
#            within one.
#   line 22  ENCLOSING SCOPE — an occurrence inside an operand restates one
#            written outside the fragment, because the outer state is on every
#            path into the branch.
figdown 0.4 sequence
title "Restatement is still refused where the paths are not exclusive"
lifeline c "Client"
state c "INIT"
state c "INIT"
state c "REQUESTING"
fragment f "which way?" type=alt
operand one "first" in=f
state c "BOUND" in=one
state c "BOUND" in=one
operand two "second" in=f
state c "REQUESTING" in=two
